      "description": "REC Power, formerly REC Solar, is a nationwide independent power producer that develops and acquires, finances, owns, operates and services distributed power assets spanning solar, battery storage, fuel cells, microgrids and gensets for commercial, industrial, institutional and public-sector customers. Founded in 1997, the platform reports more than 700 projects across 29 states and, after a July 2026 acquisition, more than 410 MW of operating assets across 25 states. Duke Energy completed the sale of its commercial distributed-generation business, including REC Solar, to an ArcLight-managed investment fund in October 2023. REC Power states that it remains owned by ArcLight Capital Partners, and ArcLight attributes the investment to Fund VII. Public sources do not disclose the platform-level stake or legal acquisition vehicle.",
